          "title": "Accept an explicit leading + sign in duration strings",
          "body": "ms('+1h') returned undefined while ms('-1h') worked. Allow an optional + in the number and add tests for it.",
          "edits": [
            {
              "op": "replace",
              "file": "index.js",
              "find": "var match = /^(-?(?:\\d+)?\\.?\\d+) *(",
              "with": "var match = /^([-+]?(?:\\d+)?\\.?\\d+) *("
            },
            {
              "op": "append",
              "file": "tests.js",
              "content": "\n// signed strings\n\ndescribe('ms(signed string)', function() {\n  it('should accept an explicit leading +', function() {\n    expect(ms('+1h')).to.be(3600000);\n    expect(ms('+1.5 days')).to.be(129600000);\n    expect(ms('+.5s')).to.be(500);\n  });\n\n  it('should still reject a lone sign', function() {\n    expect(isNaN(ms('+'))).to.be(true);\n  });\n});\n"
            }
          ],
          "note": "ms keeps every test in the root tests.js, so new tests have to be appended there. The tamper check now treats any edit to an existing test file (including one named by package.json scripts) as tampering and asks the client, so an honest improvement here still goes to P3 rather than releasing on a test the payee wrote. Conservative by design.",
